cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper below."
title: "DIFair: unified differential item functioning and algorithmic fairness auditing for educational data"
abstract: >-
  DIFair unifies differential item functioning (DIF) procedures from
  educational measurement with algorithmic fairness metrics from machine
  learning in a single Python API, and attributes a group disparity in a
  system's decisions to the pipeline stage that produced it by exact Shapley
  decomposition. It covers dichotomous and ordered categorical items,
  replicate-weight variance and plausible-value combination for large-scale
  assessments, and ships a zero-install browser front end.
